<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andrew Rutherford, 1st Earl of Teviot</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1664</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Earl of Teviot</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andrew Rutherford, 1st Earl of Teviot, was a Scottish soldier who served in the French army and as governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dunkirk">Dunkirk</a> before Charles II made him governor of English <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tangier">Tangier</a> in 1663. He began the great mole and new defences of the port, but was killed with many of his men in an ambush by Moroccan forces outside the town in 1664.</p></div>
